[CR CR1506r2 for 38.331] Reason for change: According to agreed RRC CR (R2-2002102) in RAN2 #109e, ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity is added in RACH-ConfigCommon. According to the cover sheet of agreed CR (R2-2002102) the intention is to configure ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity in SIB 1 i.e. in RACH-ConfigCommon of initial UL BWP only. This should be clarified in specification. Additionally, RACH prioritization parameters included in ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity are applicable for SpCell only as CBRA is not supported for SCell. Summary of change: Clarified that ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity is configured in RACH-ConfigCommon and RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA of only initial UL BWP. If configured, it is applied for prioritized random access procedure on any UL BWP of SpCell. Clarified that ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity is configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA of only initial UL BWP. If configured, it is applied for prioritized random access procedure on any UL BWP of SpCell. Consequences if not approved: Unecessary signaling overhead; Ambiguity in selection of RACH prioritisation parameters if ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentity is signaled in multiple UL BWPs.

